question_text:
Consider the reaction: $\text{Cl}_2(aq) + \text{H}_2\text{S}(aq) \rightarrow \text{S}(s) + 2\text{H}^+(aq) + 2\text{Cl}^-(aq)$. The rate equation is: $\text{rate} = k[\text{Cl}_2][\text{H}_2\text{S}]$. Which of these mechanisms is/are consistent with this rate equation?

(A) $\text{Cl}_2 + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{H}^+ + \text{Cl}^- + \text{Cl}^+ + \text{HS}^-\ (\text{slow})$;
$\text{Cl}^+ + \text{HS}^- \rightarrow \text{H}^+ + \text{Cl}^- + \text{S}\ (\text{fast})$

(B) $\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{H}^+ + \text{HS}^-\ (\text{fast equilibrium})$;
$\text{Cl}_2 + \text{HS}^- \rightarrow 2\text{Cl}^- + \text{H}^+ + \text{S}\ (\text{slow})$
